## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | .github/workflows/ci.yml | 🚨 blocking structural guard test test ci pty aot seam test dart still pins fa local bundle bin fah — red ci on this head the pr renames the bundle binary to fa in ci yml but the structural lint guarding this exact handoff gh 1300 artifact→shard exec bit restore → fail loud smoke → fa bin asserts the old name verified by running it on this pr head dart test test ci pty aot seam test dart ❌ the shard restores the exec bit after the download expected a value greater than 5 actual 1 ← no step contains chmod x fa local bundle bin fah any more ❌ the smoke still fails loud after the restore before fa bin expected contains test x fa local bundle bin fah actual test x fa local bundle bin fa n fa local bundle bin fa version n error 2 tests passed 2 failed fix in test ci pty aot seam test dart — use two bundle name constants 1 the pty integration linux ci yml group must assert on fa local bundle bin fa — the exec bit restore test x and version smoke lines this pr renamed 2 the nightly group keeps fa local bundle bin fah and its contains dart build cli target bin fah dart assertion line 142 nightly yml deliberately still builds bin fah dart internal never renamed self consistent blindly renaming the single bundlebin constant would break the nightly group instead 3 refresh the stale gh 1300 header comment lines 4–6 which still cites test x fa local bundle bin fah context the rest of the workflow guard suite is green on this head — 350 tests across 17 structural files ci binaries arch gate test release hygiene test nightly desktop leg guard test … all pass this is the only breakage |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

$archive = Join-Path $env:TEMP "fa-windows-$archName.zip"
$extractDir = Join-Path $env:TEMP "fa-extract-$(Get-Random)"
Write-Info "Downloading Fa for windows-$archName..."
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -OutFile $archive -UseBasicParsing -MaximumRedirection 5
try {
    # dart build cli produces: bundle/{bin/fa.exe, lib/*.dll}
    # We rename it to fa.exe and extract into the install directory.
    Expand-Archive -Path $archive -DestinationPath $extractDir -Force
    $bundleDir = Join-Path $extractDir "bundle"
    $srcExe = Join-Path $bundleDir "bin\fa.exe"
    if (-not (Test-Path $srcExe)) {
        # Older bundles shipped the binary as fah.exe.
        $srcExe = Join-Path $bundleDir "bin\fah.exe"
    }
    if (-not (Test-Path $srcExe)) {
        $listing = @(
            Get-ChildItem $bundleDir -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
                ForEach-Object { $_.FullName.Substring($bundleDir.Length + 1) }
        )
        throw "the downloaded bundle has no bin\fa.exe (contents: $($listing -join ', '))"
    }

